Sheesh, why not just end the game when you find one of the good ones?
The game balance in this game is messed up enough as it is.  You nearly
always die before a certain point (level 14 or thereabouts) and nearly
always ascend after that point.  After the castle level the game is one
big yawner, usually.

Adding superpowerful stuff (options on everything, new weapons, armor,
amulets, etc.) makes the latter half of the game even duller.  The thing
I liked best about Moria was that even superpowerful characters are
still vulnerable, cause there's no resistance to poison gas.  In nethack
high level characters are closer to Sherman Tanks than adventurers.  
Knowing you can only be killed by getting surrounded by _huge_ mobs 
makes individual monsters really useless.  "Oh, look, Demogorgon. <yawn>"

